        "body": "GenomeSpy for Python 0.9.0 upgrades the bundled renderer and generated grammar to GenomeSpy Core 1.3.0.\n\n### New authoring support\n\n- Figwig lazy data sources, branch and values transforms, category and interactive legend selections, categorical grouping and zooming, dendrogram domain outputs, and rule fills and borders.\n- Generated public schema-class exports alongside the existing Python builders. New schema features are discovered by the generator rather than added individually by hand.\n\n### Fixes and compatibility\n\n- Adopt upstream fixes for shared hover, categorical-domain updates and multi-column legends.\n- Preserve nested branch transforms and container union annotations in generated APIs.\n- Reuse checked schema setup to speed repeated serialization while retaining validation of every instance and changed custom schemas.\n- Empty ungrouped aggregates now emit zero-valued rows; selection projection follows the expanded Core grammar.\n- Retain v0.8.1's native notebook sizing fixes. Straight-link SVG exports, zero-height dendrogram viewports and exact brush-boundary matching remain known upstream limitations. Additional Scanpy integration workflows using the new capabilities remain separate work.\n\n```sh\npip install --upgrade genome-spy-python\n```\n\n[Documentation](https://genomespy.app/genome-spy-python/) · [Full changelog](https://github.com/genome-spy/genome-spy-python/compare/v0.8.1...v0.9.0)\n",
